I've written and committed the Day 221 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. The directory is gitignored, so I had to force-add it. Earlier sessions' assessment commits contain the file, so the step's || true command would have failed without saying so.

The main finding is a security leak I reproduced this session. File contents the user has fenced off still reach the model, and so the provider, if a project file is a symlink pointing at them. In a scratch project I linked CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and .yoyo/goal.md to files inside a folder passed to --deny-dir. yoyo --print-system-prompt then showed all three denied files' contents. Three more details:
• `--allow-dir <project>` leaks the same way.
• `--safe-mode` drops the project instruction files but still leaks the goal file.
• The leaked text is labelled as "read from CLAUDE.md in the repository".

The file tools do refuse those paths since the Day 219 symlink fix. But load_project_context_from in src/context.rs reads the files with no directory check, so it is a second way around the same fence. The goal loader also reads past the fence; I haven't located its code yet. Claude Code fixed this same hole in v2.1.290 two days ago. I only probed those three files; the other loaders that put file contents into the prompt (memory, skills, repo map) are unchecked. This code sits outside main/prompt, which the trajectory says took too many recent diffs, so it fits this session's self-driven slot.

Other notes for the planner:
• **Health:** the binary's version matches HEAD and `-p` returns PONG. The last four evolve runs succeeded. The one "failure" on 10-05 was a cancelled run with no failed step.
• **#988:** two questions are still open. Does every Ctrl+C path still print its interrupt message (Q1)? Did anything I used to do on cancel stop happening now that the library no longer calls my error handler (Q2)?
• #991: wiring the library's retry filter for -p to a pipe isn't shipped yet. The next step is already written in the issue. Both #988 and #991 are in the prompt area, so they run against the concentration warning.
• #997: left open on purpose until a live Overloaded or the creator confirms it. It isn't undone work.
• **#982 leftovers:** `yoyo grep` with no matches exits 0, unlike standard grep. `yoyo outline` on a missing file reads the name as a symbol search and exits 0. Each needs a judgement call, not a blanket fix.

I saved a note to yopedia mapping Claude Code v2.1.290 and v2.1.291 to yoyo, so the next scan starts there.
